  "task": "On the USGS executive page for the 2011 Great Tohoku earthquake, report the event title and displayed coordinates. Report the MMI shown by Did You Feel It? and by ShakeMap. From Ground Failure, report the Landslide Estimate and Liquefaction Estimate area and population exposure wording. From Origin, report Review Status, Magnitude including its type, Depth, Time, and the displayed contributor.\n\nStopping condition: Stop after the event identity, both intensity values, both Ground Failure estimates, and every requested Origin-card field have been recorded.\n\nConstraints:\n- Use only the supplied USGS event page and its executive cards.\n- Keep the Did You Feel It? community intensity distinct from the ShakeMap estimated intensity.\n- Keep the landslide and liquefaction area/population statements paired with the correct estimate.\n- Take Origin values from the labeled Origin card; do not substitute approximate values from the narrative tectonic summary.",
